---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { PROPERTIES } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Start a diagnostic"
  description="Diagnostic intake for Texas Movement Consulting opens soon. Here's what the 30-Day Systems & AI Diagnostic covers and how to reach us once intake is live."
  path="/start"
>
  <style>
    .status-badge {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 6px 14px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
      background: var(--panel);
      font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .status-badge::before {
      content: "";
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--tension);
      flex: none;
    }

    /* Semantically an h2 (no h2 precedes it on this page, so h1 -> h2 keeps
       heading order valid) but sized like the .panel-highlight h3 treatment
       used elsewhere on this site. */
    .panel-highlight-title {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
  </style>

  <section id="start-status" class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">START A DIAGNOSTIC</div>
        <h1>Diagnostic intake opens soon.</h1>
        <div class="status-badge">Not yet accepting live submissions</div>
        <p>
          We&rsquo;re still finishing verification of the consulting inbox this site would route requests to, so this
          page does not have a working intake form yet. We&rsquo;d rather show you that plainly than collect a brief
          that goes nowhere.
        </p>
        <p>
          When intake opens, starting an engagement will work the same way it does today in conversation: a short
          scoped brief covering your context, constraints, and what a good outcome looks like, followed by a 30-Day
          Systems &amp; AI Diagnostic.
        </p>
        <p>
          In the meantime, the fastest way to see if this is a fit is to review how engagements are structured below,
          or read the <a href="/#faq">FAQ</a> for how the work is scoped.
        </p>
        <p class="cta-link">
          <a href="/#engagements">See engagement tiers &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="panel-highlight">
        <h2 class="panel-highlight-title">What the 30-Day Diagnostic covers.</h2>
        <p>
          Maps how work, information, and money move through your company. Identifies friction, owner-dependence, and
          critical failure points. Returns a prioritized systems plan with timelines, owners, and key decisions.
        </p>
        <p class="price-line" style="color:#5c4029;">$1,500&ndash;$3,000 &middot; one-time &middot; 30 days.</p>
        <p>
          This is a description of the offer, not a live order form &mdash; nothing submitted on this page is sent
          anywhere yet.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight section--panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">KEYNOTE SPEAKING</div>
      <h2>Looking for a keynote instead?</h2>
      <p>
        Keynote and live speaking engagements run through founder Alexander Mathai&rsquo;s own site, which has its own
        contact process.
      </p>
      <p class="cta-link">
        <a href={PROPERTIES.founder.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Go to AlexanderMathai.com for keynote speaking &rarr;
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
